#VERSION 1.5.0 Paper publication release
Feature: added Sequential Binding Sites model (two to four sites)
Feature: added Null model binding assessment with Null prediction overlay and Modify Assessment override
Feature: added profile-likelihood uncertainty estimation
Feature: added parameter correlation matrix (bootstrap only)
Feature: added AIC information criteria for model comparison
Feature: added global fitting Offset constraint option
Feature: added linked temperature calculation for affinity
Feature: added selectable injection bookkeeping: MicroCal, Ideal continuous mixing and Discrete displacement
Feature: added warnings for parameters at fitting boundaries
Feature: added molar RMSD and c-values to results
Feature: saved Analysis Results can be updated with new uncertainty estimates
Feature: added Analysis Report with preview, saved reports and PDF export
Feature: added optional automated report interpretation (online service, OpenAI or Mistral AI)
Feature: added Project Information and Traceability Mode
Feature: added Origin .opj, TA NanoITC .nitc and .dh integrated-heat imports
Feature: integrated-heat imports accept absolute or normalized heats in any heat unit
Feature: added tandem detection prompt, model-free mixing criterion and back-mixing for up to five experiments
Feature: added Final Figure font choice, tick options and observations-only model selection
Feature: added Celsius/Kelvin and molar energy unit choices to exports
Feature: added ordered undo, drag-to-reorder, copy/paste and file drop onto the data list
Feature: added Experiment Designer noise levels and adjustable result table column widths
Feature: update check now uses GitHub releases
Change: concentration uncertainty is resampled from a lognormal distribution
Change: stricter Nelder-Mead convergence and faster sequential and two-site fitting
Change: integrated-heat uncertainty is weighted by contributing durations
Change: exports, graphs and reports always use period decimals
Change: projects are saved only as .ftxtc; .ftitc files can still be opened
Change: removed the asymmetric least squares baseline
Change: updated Avalonia to 12.1.4; workflow navigation moved into the macOS title bar
Science: corrected Kd,app, weighted AIC and the salt-dependence slope
Science: heat direction now follows the raw integrated peak area
Science: corrected bootstrap temperature uncertainty and percentile confidence bounds
Science: aligned the proton sign and buffer enthalpy convention across all outputs
Science: fixed buffer ionic-strength correction convergence
Fix: buffer reference changes now invalidate dependent processing and fits
Fix: hardened project saving and preserved processing metadata on reopen
Fix: fixed PEAQ, TA and integrated-heat import issues
Fix: many layout, export and Final Figure fixes on both desktop apps

